From 86b00346138bb17c1f55f8066a5c41699c141f0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 22:57:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DVLayerMerge: the comment names the FFmpeg patch by its
 number in the tree, ffmpeg-9930

The patch of libavformat that groups a Dolby Vision enhancement track in
an HEVC sample entry is ffmpeg-9930 in the LibreELEC tree: 9923 was
already taken there by another patch of FFmpeg.
---
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVLayerMerge.h | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVLayerMerge.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVLayerMerge.h
index df89bc3..b822023 100644
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVLayerMerge.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDDemuxers/DVLayerMerge.h
@@ -122,7 +122,7 @@ public:
    * libavformat groups them by the Dolby Vision descriptor of the enhancement track of a
    * transport stream, or by the stream numbers of a Blu-ray stream; by the 'vdep' reference of
    * an MP4 enhancement track with its record, in a Dolby Vision sample entry or (Hades,
-   * ffmpeg-9923) in an HEVC one ('hvc1', 'hev1') with a reference to one track only; and in Matroska,
+   * ffmpeg-9930) in an HEVC one ('hvc1', 'hev1') with a reference to one track only; and in Matroska,
    * which has no such reference, by the Dolby Vision record of the enhancement track when there
    * is exactly one other HEVC track. For MP4 and Matroska the enhancement track must also have
    * the size of an enhancement layer of the base track.
-- 
